Z||000003||JetroGT||10-08-2001||08:11 AM||||Be prepaired to spend some $$. But once you get the bugs worked out and all the matinence done it's a very reliable car. <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/NewSigt.jpg">  <BR>I work where all the missing paperclips go.<BR>Wanted: 86/87 Red GT, auto, pw, pl, pm, rear defrost,pt, Gray int, Spoiler. May be willing to trade the blue car.||||reg||1
Z||000004||grinthock||10-08-2001||08:45 AM||||Out of all the vehicles I have owned the fiero is about average if not below average on the maintenance side, KEEP IN MIND, they are upwards of 16 YEARS old (pretty cool no rust after 16 yrs!) so whatever you get will need something done.<P>Engine work is a breeze, and the car is highly modifiable, accessorizeable, and the group that comes with the car (US!) is (usually) a GREAT folk.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Smoooooth GT||10-08-2001||09:08 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by PenelopeB:<BR><B>Hi, I'm here in Southern California and just recently Fiero's have caught my eye. I've seen a couple around, a red one and a nice looking (and loud!) black one zooming about. Now I'm just starting out so I was wondering if all of you could help me out in the ups and downs of Fieros. I would appreciate any advice. Thanks a lot! <P>Hi, welcome to the forum...  you ask and we'll answer... these are the GREATEST People in the world(barring a few)...lol <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>NOS Injected 2.8L V/6<BR>UNDER CONSTRUCTION   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smooth_sig2_4_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Old Lar||10-08-2001||09:54 AM||||Up side.  A real fun car to drive, there is more room inside than it looks. It is a comfortable car to drive or ride in. They are an unusual car design with the mid engine.  They have style and any more a rare car to see on the road.  These cars can be modified with newer engines from 3.1L, 3.4L, 3800 series II, 3800 series II S/C engines and all sorts of V8s.  Expect to pay $3-8 K for such upgrades.<P>Down side.. The newest car is a 1988 or 13 years old.(Keep that in mind). Many used Fieros have high milage. Any 13-18 year old car requires maintenance. Many have been abused. Parts may be hard to find especially for the 88 suspension components.  Working on them youself, unless you have the experience will be a challenge. The Fiero does not come with power steering as a factory option, so steering is "heavy" when the car is not moving.<P>If you find a well maintained Fiero or a low milage Fiero you can have a good experience. There are many nice cars out there, but there is a lot of parts cars (junk) out there. If you go to a reputable vendor that specializes in Fieros you can locate a good Fiero.  There are several vendors in California.  Expect to pay several thousand $$ for a good Fiero.  If you find a cheap one, you get what you pay for.<P>Determine what you want in the car and how you want to use it.  In its stock form, the 4 cylinder coupes are nice driving cars, not street dragsters.  The stock V6s are not going to be the fastest car on the road either. The Fieros handle very nicely on twisty roads.<P>I've owned my 87 GT since new and my 88 GT since 96.  Both are fun.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Fiero5||10-08-2001||11:43 AM||||They are very reliable and easy to fix and maintain. The costs to fix and repair are not any more than any other car, and in many cases a lot less. The other plus for me anyway, is that I don't see tons of them everywhere I go like you do with Mustangs, Corvettes, Camaros, Firebirds and the like. It's a unique automobile that has it's mark in automotive history for many things, including the only American made mid engine car.<P>It;s looks are timeless, and you can do a lot to it very easily and usually somewhat cost effective to customize it to your liking.<P>There are many scources for Fiero extras and parts. In addition to many on the forum who have and sell parts, you can check with other vendors like <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>www.rodneydickman.com</A>  for many unique accessories, as well as, usefull and needed replacement parts. There is also Bob Parker at Kick Hill Farms in Lebanon CT who has a huge 3 story barn full of Fiero parts of every part of the car imagineable. His number is 860-642-4362. If you ever get a chance to visit his place, it has been described as a Fiero candy store. Having 12 Fieros, my family and I use Rodney Dickman and Bob Parker for many, many of our Fiero needs and highly recommend them for any of your Fiero needs. There are quite a few Fiero vendors, but these are the two we use the most. Another good source of info for parts is the Big Fiero parts book. It lists a lot of Fiero vendors and Kit manufacturers in it.<P>Keep looking around Pennocks and on the web, and you will see a full spread of what is possoble with a Fiero from the stock to the outrageouse full mods and everything in between.<P>Welcome to Fieros and to the forum, and I know that we all look forward to hearing from you again soon and seeing in the near future your "new" Fiero(s).<P>Steve Kelley<BR>Plainfield, NH<P>------------------<BR>                                <IMG SRC="http://a1040.g.akamai.net/f/1040/759/1h/206.29.192.139/info/pics/sept11.jpg">                             <BR>http://www.kelleyfamilyfieros.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||6
Z||000008||PenelopeB||10-08-2001||01:04 PM||||You guys are great! I posted this yesterday and now I have so much information!! Thanks everyone I'm so glad I came here for my questions and I'm sure there will be some more soon! Thanks Again,||||reg||10
Z||000009||Sootah||10-08-2001||11:24 PM||||I've been converted to them for a while now. But just barely got one. Sweet Black 85 GT. If Vegas isn't a terribly long drive for you I'd look for one there. Cars in general are cheaper there, and the dry climate will insure that you will have no rust. (Panels don't, there made of enduraflex, but the frame can) <P>Try <A HREF="http://www.autotrader.com" TARGET=_blank>www.autotrader.com</A>  and autos.recycler.com Tons of Fieros in your area as well as Vegas. Have a looksie. Oh, the mall is also here for you, you may find one in there.<P>As far as any odd Fiero-specific parts you may need. That's a sinch. Once again, the mall. Were all pretty tight-knit here so you can get parts for really cheap or just for the cost of shipping. 'Nuff ramblin.<P><B><I>Peace -Sootah</B></I><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__Nuclear_Happy_Face_Sig.jpg">     <BR><sup><I>Never pull your pants down in Cosco, the dang monkeys will getcha</I></sup> <BR><sup><B>AIM</B>: KSSouter</sup>||||reg||4
Z||000010||Tigger||10-08-2001||11:33 PM||||Welcome!  Good Luck in your search!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerblue4.gif"> <BR>T-T-F-N, Ta Ta For Now!<BR><A HREF="http://www.fortunecity.com/tatooine/spielberg/241/" TARGET=_blank>Tigger's Fiero Page</A>||||reg||7
Z||000011||84Bill||10-09-2001||09:47 AM||||Welcome  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Beware if you get fieros in pairs they will multiply  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <BR>You can expect to have the usual problems associated with an older car (unless you got it from a fanatic) BUT if you enjoy the car as much as the majority of people here do it's not a problem to dip into the pocket to get new stuff. The crew here on the forum is dynamite. <BR>The tech section is top notch TheOgre is very meticulous about accurate information.<BR>General Fiero is great fo upcoming events.<BR>O/T is good for laughs and other tidbits<BR>The Mall is a great place to find parts  <P>BTW<BR>I have 4 Fieros all are 4 cyl models and I have not paid more than 500 for any of them  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000012||isthiswhereiputausername?||10-09-2001||09:53 AM||||Welcome to the forum!<P>Do you have a fiero yet? if not, what kind are you interested in?  Notchback or fastback?<P>I am sure whatever one you have first you will hold onto for awhile  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I had my 84se for 10 years now and no plans to get rid of it..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
